Screens: /PurchaseFarmersEntries = all farmers' ledger entries of the business year; buttons beside the title lead to
  /PurchaseIndividual, /PurchaseGroup (purchase groups: the deals) and /PurchaseGroup/<num> (one deal: its farmers + their ledger, the "Group Ledger" button/dropdown).
  /PurchaseIndividual (sidebar: opens under "Purchase Farmers Entries" on hover) = purchase_individuals: ONE form (+add / +edit, "Save & add another") with the purchase_group columns (date, village, grain,
  rate, pay after, terms) and the purchase_farmers_entries columns (farmer, labour group, bags, kilos, handful bags, raw weight, quality, store, borrowed)
  together and ONE description. One row per farmer entry, no purchase_group. It is part of the farmer ledger: shown on /PurchaseFarmersEntries, in the
  farmer statement, in dues and payments (allocations of type 'purchase_individual'), in the year report and in the farmer analysis.
  (Not yet: loading a purchase individual's bags on a truck.)

purchase_group (deal) and its farmers:
  one village can have many purchase_group; each is a deal between the business owner and the few farmers who gathered
  Add / edit purchase_group screen: purchase_group fields on the left; on the right the owner filters the existing farmers (village, name, mobile)
  and picks the farmers taking part -> purchase_group_farmers. purchase_farmers_entries (the farmer ledger) can only be made for a listed farmer.
  If a picked farmer is already listed in another purchase_group of the SAME GRAIN (same business year) -> pop-up naming those deals; the owner must verify to go on.
  If, while editing, a listed farmer is removed -> his purchase_farmers_entries in this purchase_group are deleted with him (no pop-up, no confirmation:
  only ledger entries exist at this stage). The only refusal: an entry that is already loaded on a truck or has a payment cannot be deleted, so that farmer stays.



purchase_farmers_entries.total_available_bags = purchase_farmers_entries.no_of_filled_bags + purchase_farmers_entries.no_of_handful_bags  

total_remaining_bags <= total_available_bags
if purchase_farmer_entry_id does not exist in truck_load_lines ledger 
then truck_load_lines.total_remaining_bags = purchase_farmers_entries.total_available_bags AND truck_load_lines.no_of_loaded_bags is (initialize automatically as purchase_farmers_entries selected from select input data in UI) 
truck_load_lines.total_remaining_bags = truck_load_lines.total_remaining_bags - truck_load_lines.no_of_loaded_bags
 
bilties.total_bags_in_truck = sum of truck_load_lines.no_of_loaded_bags, for particular trip_id from different purchase_farmer_entry_id

expected_total_loaded_weight = sum of all unique (trip_id, purchase_farmer_entry_id) {(no_of_loaded_bags * expected_raw_weight_per_bag)}
difference_in_loading_weight = (merchant_total_weight - merchant_tare_weight) - expected_total_loaded_weight
average_per_bag_difference = (difference_in_loading_weight / total_bags_in_truck)
difference_in_delivering_weight = (industry_total_weight - industry_tare_weight) - (merchant_total_weight - merchant_tare_weight)
total_weight_difference = (industry_total_weight - merchant_total_weight)
tare_weight_difference = (industry_tare_weight - merchant_tare_weight)

payments.status: status IN ('partial', 'final', 'complete'), partial, last partial is called final, full for payment in signle time 

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
'farmer', 'truck', 'labour_group', 'bag_supplier', 'broker' are the party_type in payments table, and their respective id is party_id in payments table.
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
payable_amount = { ( (no_of_filled_bags * net_bag_weight ) + extra_kilos) / 20 } * grain_rate_per_20kg
farmer_total_amount = payable_amount - borrowed_amount
sum of payments.amount for (party_type = farmer, party_id = farmers.id) should not exceed (farmer_total_amount)

trip_total = { ( (industry_total_weight - industry_tare_weight) / 1000 ) * truck_trips.rent_per_ton } + { truck_trips.rent_per_bag * bilties.total_bags_in_truck }
truck_trip_total_amount = trip_total - advance_amount + other_payable - other_deduction
sum of payments.amount for (party_type = truck, party_id = trucks.id) should not exceed sum of truck_trip_total_amount over all truck_trips of that truck (paid to the truck owner; payment_allocations.payable_id = truck_trips.id)

payable_amount =(weighing_rate * total_available_bags) + (loading_rate * total_bags_in_truck) + (pulling_rate * total_pulled_bags) + (mixing_rate * total_mixed_bags) + (other_expenses)
labour_group_total_amount = payable_amount - borrowing_amount
sum of payments.amount for (party_type = labour_group, party_id = labour_groups.id) should not exceed (labour_group_total_amount)
business_expense_labour_day = petrol + meal

payable_amount = no_of_bags * rate_per_bag 
bag_supply_total_amount = payable_amount
sum of payments.amount for (party_type = bag_supplier, party_id = bag_suppliers.id) should not exceed (bag_supply_total_amount)

brokerage_amount = total_bags_in_truck * brokerage_per_bag 
broker_total_amount = brokerage_amount
sum of payments.amount for (party_type = broker, party_id = brokers.id) should not exceed (broker_total_amount)

